e] [17592186301238 1089 "q-332376" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301238 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534647 true] [17592186301238 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=9x-3.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{3x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301238 1113 #uuid "fc235b3a-1731-5566-a624-628471650abf" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301238 1145 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}-3{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha x+\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\alpha -3(\\alpha x+\\beta )=9x-3\n$$\n\nWe then group the terms on the left-hand side, as follows:\n\n$$\n-3\\alpha x+(\\alpha -3\\beta )=9x-3\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-3\\alpha =9\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ \\alpha -3\\beta =-3\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-3,\\,\\beta =0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-3x.\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nthe general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{3x}-3x.\n$$" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301240 13194139534647 true] [17592186301239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301241 13194139534647 true] [17592186301239 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534647 true] [17592186301239 1041 "field-1" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301239 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301241 13194139534647 true] [17592186301239 1110 #uuid "44504acb-40f3-5cc4-ad0e-151cd18d2e33" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301240 1034 "Ae^{3x}+3x" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301240 1111 #uuid "a145f527-5c8e-5e9c-8126-676a9617c31d" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301241 1034 "Ae^{3x}-3x" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301241 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301241 1111 #uuid "b4fb5d74-8054-59d8-a0aa-af0380bf1c10" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301242 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301243 13194139534647 true] [17592186301242 1089 "q-332547" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301242 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534647 true] [17592186301242 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6y=-30.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-6x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301242 1113 #uuid "0437cac1-0430-51b8-a73f-f9f901b83c52" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301242 1145 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n5\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}+6{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-6x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\beta $ is a constant to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=0.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n5\\cdot 0+6\\beta =-30\n$$\n\nSolving this equation gives $\\beta =-5.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-5.\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nthe general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-6x}-5.\n$$" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301243 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301244 13194139534647 true] [17592186301243 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534647 true] [17592186301243 1041 "field-1" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301243 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301244 13194139534647 true] [17592186301243 1110 #uuid "f6e0f49b-23d4-525a-8baa-9e59b924e623" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301244 1034 "Ae^{-6x}-5" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301244 1111 #uuid "4b7489ad-303a-579f-8d97-f60645cc3f97" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301245 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301246 13194139534647 true] [17592186301245 1089 "q-332556" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301245 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534647 true] [17592186301245 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y=-{x}^{2}+6x-7.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant." 13194139534647 true] [17592186301245 1113 #uuid "ce3e0989-e7de-5d8b-bc2e-aea033858039" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301245 1145 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}-{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta $, and $\\gamma $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha x+\\beta .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta ,$ and $\\gamma ,$  we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(2\\alpha x+\\beta )-(\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}+6x-7\n$$\n\nWe then group the terms on the left-hand side, as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\alpha {x}^{2}+(2\\alpha -\\beta )x+(\\beta -\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}+6x-7\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-\\alpha =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,{x}^{2}) \\\\ 2\\alpha -\\beta =6\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ \\beta -\\gamma =-7\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =1,\\beta =-4,\\gamma =3.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={x}^{2}-4x+3.\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}\n$$\n\nthe general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x}+{x}^{2}-4x+3.\n$$" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301247 13194139534647 true] [17592186301246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301248 13194139534647 true] [17592186301246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301249 13194139534647 true] [17592186301246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301250 13194139534647 true] [17592186301246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301251 13194139534647 true] [17592186301246 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534647 true] [17592186301246 1041 "selection" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301246 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301247 13194139534647 true] [17592186301246 1110 #uuid "595bef39-61a0-5f5b-9dd1-0332bad33c71" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301247 1034 "y=A{e}^{x}+{x}^{2}-4x+3" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301247 1111 #uuid "3c9118bc-ed65-5ad8-905d-c0def882717f" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301248 1034 "y=A{e}^{x}+{x}^{2}-4x-3" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301248 1111 #uuid "75e06894-732c-54e4-b86f-e8d71ccb76ab" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301249 1034 "y=A{e}^{x}-{x}^{2}-4x+3" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301249 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301249 1111 #uuid "8195fd33-4ab7-5e3b-84f6-7ede3d063976" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301250 1034 "y=A{e}^{x}+2{x}^{2}-4x+3" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301250 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301250 1111 #uuid "7ece337a-30e2-5059-a6a1-fdab3768f67b" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301251 1034 "y=A{e}^{x}+{x}^{2}-2x+3" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301251 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301251 1111 #uuid "1318eef8-93f7-570e-aa25-456973883908" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301252 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301253 13194139534647 true] [17592186301252 1089 "q-332704" 13194139534647 true] [175921863