ate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}_{c}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}=-9\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}_{c}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int -9\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}_{c}}\\,\\text{d}{y}_{c} & =\\int -9\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|{y}_{c}| & =-9x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we make ${y}_{c}$ the subject by exponentiating both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{y}_{c}| & ={e}^{-9x+C} \\\\  & ={e}^{-9x}{e}^{C} \\\\  & =K{e}^{-9x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}.$ \n\nFinally, we can drop the absolute value by allowing the arbitrary constant to be either positive or negative, i.e., setting $A=\\pm K.$  Therefore, the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-9x},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant." 13194139534647 true] [17592186301260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301261 13194139534647 true] [17592186301260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301262 13194139534647 true] [17592186301260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301263 13194139534647 true] [17592186301260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301264 13194139534647 true] [17592186301260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301265 13194139534647 true] [17592186301260 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534647 true] [17592186301260 1041 "selection" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301260 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301263 13194139534647 true] [17592186301260 1110 #uuid "482e4922-b9f8-5421-a3d1-5a087d4d4c3e" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301261 1034 "A{e}^{18x}" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301261 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301261 1111 #uuid "d539de16-5135-5bb9-a8c2-da4a0ba70dea" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301262 1034 "A{e}^{9x}" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301262 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301262 1111 #uuid "54095541-0443-5cb3-bb1a-87635bc7783a" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301263 1034 "A{e}^{-9x}" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301263 1103 #edb/ref 