\n{y}_{c}^{′}+2{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta ,$ and $\\gamma $ are constants to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha x+\\beta .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta ,$ and $\\gamma ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(2\\alpha x+\\beta )+2(\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma )=4{x}^{2}-3x+2.\n$$\n\nWe then group the terms on the left-hand side, as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\alpha {x}^{2}+(2\\alpha +2\\beta )x+(\\beta +2\\gamma )=4{x}^{2}-3x+2.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2\\alpha =4\\,(\\text{equating the coefficients of }{x}^{2}) \\\\ 2\\alpha +2\\beta =-3\\,(\\text{equating the coefficients of }x) \\\\ \\beta +2\\gamma =2\\,(\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =2,$ $\\beta =-\\frac{7}{2},$ and $\\gamma =\\frac{11}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=2{x}^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}x+\\frac{11}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}x+\\frac{11}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the constant $A$ using the initial condition.\n\nSubstituting $y(0)=-2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-2(0)}+2(0)^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}(0)+\\frac{11}{4} & =-2 \\\\ A+\\frac{11}{4} & =-2 \\\\ A & =-\\frac{19}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{19}{4}{e}^{-2x}+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}x+\\frac{11}{4}.\n$$" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301285 13194139534647 true] [17592186301284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301286 13194139534647 true] [17592186301284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301287 13194139534647 true] [17592186301284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301288 13194139534647 true] [17592186301284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301289 13194139534647 true] [17592186301284 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534647 true] [17592186301284 1041 "selection" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301284 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301287 13194139534647 true] [17592186301284 1110 #uuid "b584940c-7b63-53ec-9eb0-ef15f5f8f1a8" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301285 1034 "y=-9{e}^{-2x}-2{x}^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}x+7" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301285 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301285 1111 #uuid "c4f14d54-3b68-5511-8ebc-94d7e7ef9dac" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301286 1034 "y=-4{e}^{-2x}+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}x+2" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301286 1111 #uuid "ab98b9dc-9aae-5305-b1fa-80643f1ad078" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301287 1034 "y=-\\frac{19}{4}{e}^{-2x}+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}x+\\frac{11}{4}" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301287 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301287 1111 #uuid "e7d56cee-26d5-5eb4-9240-95543d131e87" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301288 1034 "y=-\\frac{9}{4}{e}^{-2x}+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}x+\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301288 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301288 1111 #uuid "a92e6602-1191-5eac-9b37-fe6411e0efa4" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301289 1034 "y=\\frac{19}{4}{e}^{-2x}+2{x}^{2}+\\frac{7}{2}x-\\frac{11}{4}" 13194139534647 true] [17592186301289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534647 true] [17592186301289 1111 #uuid "b1a8d3ed-b266-59a6-b7ec-7c53ccc470a